{
  "$defs": {
    "AeCell": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Actual versus expected for one level of one factor (FR-MODEL-50).\n\n`ci_95` is on the **ratio**, not on the actual: an A/E of 1.19 whose interval excludes\n1.0 is a finding, and one whose interval spans it is noise. Without the interval the\ntwo render identically, which is how a thin cell becomes a rating decision.",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "ae": {
          "title": "Ae",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "ci_95": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "maxItems": 2,
              "minItems": 2,
              "prefixItems": [
                {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                {
                  "type": "number"
                }
              ],
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Ci 95"
        },
        "expected": {
          "title": "Expected",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "exposure_years": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "description": "Exact decimal as a string; never a binary float (FR-OVR-7).",
              "pattern": "^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Exposure Years"
        },
        "factor": {
          "title": "Factor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "level": {
          "title": "Level",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor",
        "level",
        "actual",
        "expected",
        "ae"
      ],
      "title": "AeCell",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "CalibrationBin": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Predicted against observed within a predicted-decile bin (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "bin": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Bin",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "predicted": {
          "title": "Predicted",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "bin",
        "rows",
        "predicted",
        "actual"
      ],
      "title": "CalibrationBin",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ComplexityDiagnostic": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Factor and parameter counts against whatever thresholds are in force (FR-MODEL-81).\n\nRecorded on **every** fit. The thresholds are stored with the measurements because they\nare workspace settings that change: a fit judged against no limit and a fit judged\nagainst a limit of 40 are different events, and a diagnostic that stored only the\ncounts would render them identically a year later.",
      "properties": {
        "claims_per_parameter": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Claims Per Parameter"
        },
        "exposure_per_parameter": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Exposure Per Parameter"
        },
        "factor_count": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Factor Count",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "max_factor_count": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Max Factor Count"
        },
        "min_exposure_per_parameter": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Min Exposure Per Parameter"
        },
        "parameter_count": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Parameter Count",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor_count",
        "parameter_count"
      ],
      "title": "ComplexityDiagnostic",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "FeatureImportance": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One feature's importance under the three measures a booster already knows.\n\nAll three, because they disagree and the disagreement is the information: `gain` says\nhow much a split improved the objective, `cover` how much data it improved it over, and\n`frequency` merely how often the feature was chosen. A feature that is frequent and\nlow-gain is one the model reaches for and learns little from — invisible if only one\nmeasure is stored.",
      "properties": {
        "cover": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 0.0,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Cover"
        },
        "feature": {
          "title": "Feature",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "frequency": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Frequency",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "gain": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Gain",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "feature",
        "gain",
        "frequency"
      ],
      "title": "FeatureImportance",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GbmDiagnostics": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "GBM-specific evidence (FR-MODEL-52), all six things the requirement names.\n\nThe evaluation curve is here rather than on `GbmFitResult` because FR-MODEL-52 calls it\na diagnostic and asks for **train and holdout** — which is FR-MODEL-54's shape, and the\nshape `diagnostics.schema.json` has carried since Phase 0. `fit_gbm` produces it and\nhands it back for the caller to place here; only `best_iteration` stays on the fit,\nbecause scoring needs it and diagnostics are not loaded to score.",
      "properties": {
        "eval_curve": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/GbmEvalPoint"
          },
          "title": "Eval Curve",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "importances": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/FeatureImportance"
          },
          "title": "Importances",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "max_depth": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Max Depth",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "mean_depth": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Mean Depth",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "monotonicity": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/MonotonicityCheck"
          },
          "title": "Monotonicity",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "partial_dependence": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PartialDependence"
          },
          "title": "Partial Dependence",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "permutation_importances": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PermutationImportance"
          },
          "title": "Permutation Importances",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "tree_count": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Tree Count",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "tree_count",
        "max_depth",
        "mean_depth"
      ],
      "title": "GbmDiagnostics",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GbmEvalPoint": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One row of the evaluation curve FR-MODEL-52 requires (FR-MODEL-30 persists it).\n\nBoth partitions on one row rather than two series, because the pair is the point: a\nmetric still improving on train while flat on holdout is the shape early stopping\nexists to catch, and two separately-stored series can be joined wrongly.",
      "properties": {
        "holdout": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Holdout"
        },
        "iteration": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Iteration",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "metric": {
          "title": "Metric",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "train": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Train"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "iteration",
        "metric"
      ],
      "title": "GbmEvalPoint",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "GlmDiagnostics": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "GLM-specific evidence (FR-MODEL-51).",
      "properties": {
        "aic": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Aic"
        },
        "aliasing": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Aliasing",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "bic": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Bic"
        },
        "degrees_of_freedom": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Degrees Of Freedom",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "deviance": {
          "title": "Deviance",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "dispersion": {
          "title": "Dispersion",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "leverage_blob": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Leverage Blob"
        },
        "null_deviance": {
          "title": "Null Deviance",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "residual_blob": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Residual Blob"
        },
        "type_iii_tests": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TypeIIITest"
          },
          "title": "Type Iii Tests",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "vif": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "title": "Vif",
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "deviance",
        "null_deviance",
        "dispersion",
        "degrees_of_freedom"
      ],
      "title": "GlmDiagnostics",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "LiftBin": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One predicted-decile bin of a lift/gains curve (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "actual": {
          "title": "Actual",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "bin": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Bin",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "exposure_years": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "description": "Exact decimal as a string; never a binary float (FR-OVR-7).",
              "pattern": "^-?[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?$",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Exposure Years"
        },
        "predicted": {
          "title": "Predicted",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "bin",
        "rows",
        "predicted",
        "actual"
      ],
      "title": "LiftBin",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "MonotonicityCheck": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Whether the **fitted** response respects a declared constraint (FR-MODEL-52).\n\nVerified rather than assumed. A constraint is a parameter passed to a library, and the\nthing that makes it true of this model is that someone swept the factor and looked —\nwhich is also what `TransparencyArtifact.monotonicity_verified` reports upward (R3).",
      "properties": {
        "declared": {
          "title": "Declared",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "factor": {
          "title": "Factor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "holds": {
          "title": "Holds",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "worst_violation": {
          "default": 0.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Worst Violation",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor",
        "declared",
        "holds"
      ],
      "title": "MonotonicityCheck",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PartialDependence": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The fitted response to one factor, averaged over the book (FR-MODEL-52).\n\n`exposure_share` rides with every point because a partial dependence curve is most\ndramatic exactly where the book is thinnest, and a plot without it invites reading a\nspike over 0.2 % of exposure as a rating signal.",
      "properties": {
        "factor": {
          "title": "Factor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "points": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PartialDependencePoint"
          },
          "title": "Points",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor"
      ],
      "title": "PartialDependence",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PartialDependencePoint": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "exposure_share": {
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Exposure Share",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "mean_prediction": {
          "title": "Mean Prediction",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "value": {
          "title": "Value",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value",
        "mean_prediction",
        "exposure_share"
      ],
      "title": "PartialDependencePoint",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PartitionDiagnostics": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Every universal metric, for one partition (FR-MODEL-50).\n\nAt fit time one of these describes train and another describes holdout, and neither is\nmeaningful without the other — which is why a *fit* only ever holds them together\n(`UniversalDiagnostics`).\n\nA backtest holds exactly one (`backtests.BacktestSummary`, FR-MODEL-57), and that is not\nthe same defect: its population was never split, so there is no counterpart to withhold,\nand what it is read against is the model's own fit-time holdout on a different artifact.",
      "properties": {
        "ae_by_factor": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AeCell"
          },
          "title": "Ae By Factor",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "ae_overall": {
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "Ae Overall",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "calibration": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/CalibrationBin"
          },
          "title": "Calibration",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "gini": {
          "title": "Gini",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "gini_normalised": {
          "title": "Gini Normalised",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "lift": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/LiftBin"
          },
          "title": "Lift",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "residual_summary": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ResidualSummary"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "rows": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Rows",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "weighting": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/Weighting"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "weighting",
        "rows",
        "ae_overall",
        "gini",
        "gini_normalised"
      ],
      "title": "PartitionDiagnostics",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "PermutationImportance": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "How much the holdout metric degrades when one feature is shuffled (FR-MODEL-52).\n\nOn the **holdout**, and stated as a degradation rather than a score, because that is\nthe question an actuary is asking: what would this model lose if this variable were\nnoise. Split importance answers a different question — how the trees were built — and\na feature can be split on constantly while carrying no predictive weight.",
      "properties": {
        "baseline": {
          "title": "Baseline",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "degradation": {
          "title": "Degradation",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "feature": {
          "title": "Feature",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "permuted": {
          "title": "Permuted",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "repeats": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Repeats",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "seed": {
          "title": "Seed",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "feature",
        "baseline",
        "permuted",
        "degradation",
        "repeats",
        "seed"
      ],
      "title": "PermutationImportance",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ResidualSummary": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Distribution summary of the working residuals (FR-MODEL-50).",
      "properties": {
        "maximum": {
          "title": "Maximum",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "mean": {
          "title": "Mean",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "minimum": {
          "title": "Minimum",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "p01": {
          "title": "P01",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "p99": {
          "title": "P99",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "std": {
          "title": "Std",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "mean",
        "std",
        "minimum",
        "maximum",
        "p01",
        "p99"
      ],
      "title": "ResidualSummary",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TypeIIITest": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A factor's type-III deviance test (FR-MODEL-51).\n\n`deviance_delta` is the increase in deviance when the factor is dropped, on `df`\ndegrees of freedom — a likelihood-ratio statistic, so the p-value means what a reader\nexpects it to mean.",
      "properties": {
        "deviance_delta": {
          "title": "Deviance Delta",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "df": {
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Df",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "factor": {
          "title": "Factor",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "p_value": {
          "maximum": 1.0,
          "minimum": 0.0,
          "title": "P Value",
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "factor",
        "deviance_delta",
        "df",
        "p_value"
      ],
      "title": "TypeIIITest",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "UniversalDiagnostics": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Train and holdout, side by side (FR-MODEL-54).\n\nBoth fields are required. The requirement says a diagnostic reported without its\nholdout counterpart *is a defect*, and the cheapest way to honour that is to make the\ndefective shape unrepresentable rather than to check for it later.",
      "properties": {
        "holdout": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PartitionDiagnostics"
        },
        "train": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/PartitionDiagnostics"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "train",
        "holdout"
      ],
      "title": "UniversalDiagnostics",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Weighting": {
      "description": "How a metric was weighted (FR-MODEL-55).\n\n`EXPOSURE` for frequency and burning cost, `CLAIM_COUNT` for severity, `COUNT` where\nthe metric genuinely counts rows. The UI labels an unweighted metric on an\nexposure-weighted problem *as such* — which it can only do if the fit said which.",
      "enum": [
        "exposure",
        "count",
        "claim_count"
      ],
      "title": "Weighting",
      "type": "string"
    }
  },
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "The persisted artifact (`02` §4, `diagnostics.schema.json`).\n\nImmutable: computed at fit time and read thereafter (FR-MODEL-49).\n\n`gbm` is populated from the GBM slice on (FR-MODEL-52) and is `None` for a GLM, which\nis the honest reading of \"GBM-specific\".\n\n`cross_validation` is still declared and always `None`: FR-MODEL-53 computes it **at fit\ntime**, so this artifact is where it will land, and its producer is a later slice.\n\n**`backtest` was here and is gone (2026-08-18).** It was declared from Phase 0 and typed\n`None`, and nothing could ever have populated it. FR-MODEL-49 makes these diagnostics\ncomputed once at fit time and read thereafter, while FR-MODEL-57's backtest runs against\na *later* Dataset Version — after this artifact is written, and again for every period\nafter that, which one field has no room for. It is its own artifact (`backtests.Backtest`,\n`02` §4.12), and FR-MODEL-57 carries the amendment. The same removal, for the same\nreason, that `PartitionDiagnostics.double_lift` got.",
  "properties": {
    "complexity": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/ComplexityDiagnostic"
    },
    "computed_at": {
      "format": "date-time",
      "title": "Computed At",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "cross_validation": {
      "default": null,
      "title": "Cross Validation",
      "type": "null"
    },
    "gbm": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/GbmDiagnostics"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null
    },
    "glm": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/GlmDiagnostics"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null
    },
    "id": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "title": "Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "job_id": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "format": "uuid",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "title": "Job Id"
    },
    "model_id": {
      "format": "uuid",
      "title": "Model Id",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "universal": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/UniversalDiagnostics"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "model_id",
    "computed_at",
    "universal",
    "complexity"
  ],
  "title": "Diagnostics",
  "type": "object"
}
